  "_comment": [
    "The login backoff both backends must implement alike (BOOTSTRAP.md §5.1, issue #16).",
    "`parameters` are the §12 defaults, LOGIN_FIRST_BACKOFF and LOGIN_MAX_BACKOFF; each backend's config",
    "test holds its own defaults to them, so a default that drifts fails there.",
    "`curve`: the window after the nth consecutive failure on one key, in seconds.",
    "`keys`: the keys one failed login writes. `ip` is the client address as its connection carries it, in",
    "canonical form; each suite presents it the way its own server would (Go's RemoteAddr host:port, Tomcat's",
    "expanded IPv6) and expects this spelling back.",
    "Both suites read this file; neither keeps a copy of the numbers."
